How to Install Mekh PWA on Your Mobile Device
Introduction
Mekh is a Progressive Web App (PWA) that can be installed on your mobile device just like a regular app from the app store. Installing Mekh gives you a native app-like experience with faster loading, offline capabilities, and easy access from your home screen. This guide covers the installation process for both Android and iOS devices.

What is a PWA?
Progressive Web Apps combine the best of web and mobile apps:

Native app experience without app store downloads
Offline functionality for basic browsing
Push notifications (when implemented)
Home screen installation for quick access
Automatic updates without manual app store updates
System Requirements

Android Requirements
Chrome Browser (recommended) or Samsung Internet
Android 8.0+ (Oreo or later)
At least 50MB free storage space
Internet connection for initial installation
iOS Requirements
Safari Browser (required for installation)
iOS 16.4+ (iPhone and iPad)
At least 50MB free storage space
Internet connection for initial installation

Installation on Android Devices
Method 1: Using Chrome Browser (Recommended)
Open Chrome Browser
Launch Google Chrome on your Android device
Make sure you're using the latest version
Visit Mekh Website
Go to mekh.app
Wait for the page to fully load
Look for Install Prompt
You'll see a banner at the bottom of the screen saying "Install Mekh"
If you don't see it, tap the menu (three dots) in the top-right corner
Install the App
Tap the "Install" button in the banner, or
Tap "Add to Home screen" from the menu
Confirm the installation when prompted
Access from Home Screen
The Mekh app icon will appear on your home screen
Tap it to launch the app in standalone mode
Method 2: Using Samsung Internet Browser
Open Samsung Internet
Launch Samsung Internet browser
Navigate to mekh.app
Tap the Menu
Tap the menu button (three lines) in the bottom-right corner
Select "Add to Home screen"
Install
Confirm the installation
The app will be added to your home screen

Method 3: Manual Installation (Alternative)
If the automatic prompt doesn't appear:

Open Browser Menu
Tap the three dots menu in Chrome/Samsung Internet
Look for "Add to Home screen" or "Install app"
Add to Home Screen
Select "Add to Home screen"
Customize the app name if desired (defaults to "Mekh")
Tap "Add"
Launch from Home Screen
Find the Mekh icon on your home screen
Tap to open in app mode
Installation on iOS Devices (iPhone/iPad)
Using Safari Browser (Required)
Open Safari Browser
Safari is the only browser that supports PWA installation on iOS
Do not use Chrome, Firefox, or other browsers for installation
Visit Mekh Website
Open Safari and go to mekh.app
Wait for the page to load completely
Tap the Share Button
Look for the share icon (square with upward arrow) at the bottom of the screen
Tap it to open the share menu
Find "Add to Home Screen"
Scroll through the share options
Look for "Add to Home Screen" (may be in the second row)
Tap it
Confirm Installation
Review the app name (Mekh) and icon
Tap "Add" in the top-right corner
Access from Home Screen
The Mekh app icon will appear on your home screen
Tap it to launch the app
Troubleshooting iOS Installation
Can't find "Add to Home Screen"?

Make sure you're using Safari (not Chrome or other browsers)
Try refreshing the page and waiting for full load
Check that you're running iOS 16.4 or later
App doesn't appear on home screen?

Check all home screen pages
Try searching for "Mekh" in Spotlight search
Restart your device and check again

